<p>Compound growth is the closest thing to magic in all of money. Your money earns money, then that money earns money too, and given enough time the snowball gets absurd. The catch is that time does most of the heavy lifting, so the best day to start was years ago and the second best day is today. Run your numbers.</p>

<div class="hmca">
  <h3>The Compound Growth Calculator</h3>
  <p class="hmca-sub">See what steady investing could grow into, and how much of it is pure growth versus your own deposits.</p>

  <div class="hmca-field">
    <label>Starting amount <span class="hmca-hint">(what you have now)</span></label>
    <div class="hmca-in"><span class="pfx">$</span><input type="number" id="cgStart" min="0" step="100" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="1,000"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="hmca-field">
    <label>Added each month</label>
    <div class="hmca-in"><span class="pfx">$</span><input type="number" id="cgMonthly" min="0" step="25" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="200"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="hmca-field">
    <label>Years you will let it grow</label>
    <div class="hmca-in"><span class="pfx" style="font-size:1.3rem">yrs</span><input type="number" id="cgYears" min="1" max="70" step="1" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="30" style="padding-left:3.2rem"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="hmca-field">
    <label>Average yearly return <span class="hmca-hint">(7% is a common long-run stock estimate)</span></label>
    <div class="hmca-in"><input type="number" id="cgRate" min="0" step="0.5" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="7" style="padding-left:1rem;padding-right:2.4rem"><span class="pfx" style="left:auto;right:14px">%</span></div>
